%% DM26-0670

%% How a session ends or waits, as built (2026-11-04, docs/architecture/cassini-broker.md). A goodbye ends the session at once,
%% and any other loss keeps it for the retention window. There is no idle timeout of the broker's own: a dead connection
%% is found by TCP keepalive and TCP_USER_TIMEOUT (60 s), or by a failed write.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Client as Agent
    participant Listener
    participant LM as ListenerManager
    participant SM as SessionManager
    participant SA as SessionAgent
    participant Subs as SubscriberManager / SubscriberAgents

    alt a goodbye: a client that means it (a multi-instance pod's clean shutdown says one)
        Client->>Listener: DisconnectRequest(Goodbye)
        Listener->>LM: DisconnectRequest(Goodbye, registration_id)
        Listener->>Listener: stop
        LM->>SM: DisconnectRequest(Goodbye, registration_id)
        SM->>SA: stop
        SM->>Subs: DisconnectRequest(registration_id)
        Subs->>Subs: forget its subscriptions, which drops what they held
    else the connection is gone: EOF, an I/O error or a write that failed
        Listener->>LM: DisconnectRequest(RemoteClosed or TransportError)
        Listener->>Listener: stop
        LM->>SM: DisconnectRequest(reason, registration_id)
        SM->>SM: detach: the session is kept, with its subscribers, for the retention window
        SM->>Subs: SessionDetached
        Note over Subs: They no longer hold their topics back, and keep what they hold while the budget allows.
        alt the client comes back in time
            Client->>Listener: register, asking for this session (broker/client_reconnect)
        else the retention window passes (SessionExpiryTick)
            SM->>SA: stop
            SM->>Subs: DisconnectRequest(registration_id)
        else the budget is exhausted while it is away
            Subs->>SA: SessionShed(topic, count): they let go of what they held
            SA->>SM: EndSession(id, why)
            SM->>SA: stop, and remember why for when it comes back
            SM->>Subs: DisconnectRequest(registration_id)
        end
    else its certificate is revoked (JudgeSubscriptions, on a change of authority)
        Listener->>LM: DisconnectRequest(RemoteClosed)
        Listener->>Listener: stop
        LM->>SM: DisconnectRequest(RemoteClosed): detached
        Note over SM: Kept for the retention window, for the identity's next certificate to claim.
    else it stalled (broker/slow_subscriber_stall), or it was superseded (broker/session_supersede_takeover)
        Note over Listener,SM: Each of those has its own diagram: a stall detaches the session, and a supersede closes the old connection.
    end
